.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_DEVI_CONFIG 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_devi_config ,
.Nm ndi_devi_config_driver ,
.Nm ndi_devi_config_one ,
.Nm ndi_devi_unconfig ,
.Nm e_ddi_devi_unconfig ,
.Nm ndi_devi_unconfig_one ,
.Nm ndi_devi_unconfig_driver
.Nd configure and unconfigure the children of a nexus
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_config
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_config_driver
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fa "major_t major"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_config_one
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *devnm"
.Fa "dev_info_t **dipp"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_unconfig
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo e_ddi_devi_unconfig
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "dev_info_t **dipp"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_unconfig_one
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *devnm"
.Fa "dev_info_t **dipp"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_devi_unconfig_driver
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fa "major_t major"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dip
Parent nexus whose children are operated on.
.It Va flags
Operation flags described below.
.It Va major
Driver major number; use a valid bound driver number.
.It Va devnm
Null-terminated child name, normally in \fBname@address\fP form, relative
to the parent.
.It Va dipp
Child output for configuration, or optional failure-node output for
unconfiguration.
It is required for \fBndi_devi_config_one()\fP.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions drive configuration through a nexus driver's \fBbus_config\fP
or \fBbus_unconfig\fP entry point, using framework defaults when no suitable
entry point exists.
Configuration and the single-child unconfiguration interface require an
attached parent nexus.
Bulk unconfiguration can also remove children of a detached nexus through
the framework defaults.
.Pp
\fBndi_devi_config()\fP configures children of \fBdip\fP.
\fBndi_devi_config_driver()\fP selects the driver identified by \fBmajor\fP;
recursive configuration can also attach intermediate nexus nodes needed to
reach that driver's devices.
\fBndi_devi_config_one()\fP enumerates and attaches the child named by \fBdevnm\fP
and returns a held node in \fB*dipp\fP.
Release any returned node with \fBndi_rele_devi()\fP.
Initialize the output to \fBNULL\fP and check it even on failure: a child can be
returned when its attachment succeeded but recursive configuration failed.
.Pp
\fBndi_devi_unconfig()\fP unconfigures children of \fBdip\fP.
\fBndi_devi_unconfig_driver()\fP restricts the operation by driver major number.
\fBndi_devi_unconfig_one()\fP unconfigures the named child's descendants and then
the child itself; an absent child is treated as already unconfigured.
\fBe_ddi_devi_unconfig()\fP additionally accepts a failure-node output.
For these unconfiguration functions, a non-null \fBdipp\fP requests a held node
at which unconfiguration failed, when one is available.
Initialize \fB*dipp\fP to \fBNULL\fP before the call and release a non-null result with
\fBndi_rele_devi()\fP.
Unconfiguration can make partial progress before returning a failure.
.Pp
Common operation flags are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv NDI_CONFIG
Recursively configure descendants of nexus children.
.It Dv NDI_UNCONFIG
Unconfigure children back to the uninitialized state, releasing
resources acquired during child initialization.
.It Dv NDI_DEVI_REMOVE
Remove device nodes after unconfiguration.
.It Dv NDI_DEVI_ONLINE
Allow configuration to bring an explicitly offlined device online.
.It Dv NDI_DEVI_OFFLINE
Mark a detached device offline to prevent deferred attachment.
.It Dv NDI_NO_EVENT
Suppress device add/remove event generation.
.It Dv NDI_DEVI_DEBUG
Enable diagnostic messages for the operation.
.It Dv NDI_MTC_OFF
Disable multithreaded descendant configuration or unconfiguration.
.El
.Pp
\fBNDI_ONLINE_ATTACH\fP is retained for callers that request online attachment;
the current configuration paths attempt attachment without requiring this bit.
Other flags in the header serve internal framework paths and are not general
options for nexus drivers.
The functions manage device-tree locking, but callers must keep the input
node valid and respect ancestor-before-descendant lock ordering.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called from user or kernel context.
They may sleep.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP on success and an NDI failure
status otherwise.
Bulk configuration can succeed even if individual children do not attach
or descendant configuration fails: the default implementation attempts
available children without propagating every failure.
A successful call does not provide an atomic snapshot of the device tree.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_busop_bus_config 9F ,
.Xr ndi_devi_enter 9F ,
.Xr ndi_devi_online 9F ,
.Xr ndi_hold_devi 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
